title: find_definition

!! `find_definition` MCP Tool

Where a name is defined, found the way the running wiki finds it: wikitext definitions, and the ~JavaScript behind widgets, filter operators, run prefixes and macros. The editor's go to definition answers from the same code, see [[LSP Go to Definition]].

!! Parameters

|!Parameter |!Default |!Description |
|`name` |required |the name as written in a call; a widget keeps its `$`, as in `$list`, and a run prefix its `:`, as in `:else` |
|`filter` |`[all[shadows+tiddlers]]` |TW filter expression to scope the search for wikitext definitions |

!! Output format

```
<title>  (from <plugin>)
  <line>#<hash> [<kinds>]: <line text>
```

Kinds are `procedure`, `function`, `macro` and `widget` for a pragma, with `global` added to the one definition the wiki imports for everyone, and `JavaScript widget`, `filter operator`, `run prefix` and `JavaScript macro` for code. A tiddler a plugin supplies names that plugin; the core is never named. The anchor is what `edit_tiddler` takes as `pos`. A footer counts definitions and tiddlers, and `(no definition)` means none was found.

!! Which code is shown

The code that actually runs: a tiddler of your own overrides a plugin's shadow, which overrides the core's, and a module is matched to the running widget, operator or prefix by identity rather than by name, since a later module can take over a name.

!! Direct invocations

```
find_definition(name="list-links")
find_definition(name="$list")
find_definition(name="compare")
find_definition(name=":else")
find_definition(name="list-links", filter="[tag[$:/tags/Macro]]")
```

